  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.329,
      "text": "An octopus has three beating hearts and bright blue copper-based blood.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "iNaturalist",
        "title": "Common Octopus (Octopus vulgaris)",
        "credit": "(c) Golfopolikayak, some rights reserved (CC BY)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/299781028"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.533,
          "end": 4.333,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.329,
      "end": 12.774,
      "text": "Stepping up in scale from single-heart creatures, this soft-bodied marine genius lacks bones entirely to squeeze through tiny gaps.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Enteroctopus dofleini in aquarium crop.jpg",
        "credit": "Enteroctopus_dofleini_in_aquarium.jpg: Bachrach44\nderivative work: The High Fin Sperm Whale",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enteroctopus_dofleini_in_aquarium_crop.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.333,
          "end": 12.767,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.774,
      "end": 20.894,
      "text": "Climbing higher along the biological scale, the entire animal possesses around five hundred million total neural connections.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Cephalopoda (Plate LXXVI) (6140286962).jpg",
        "credit": "Chun, Carl",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Cephalopoda_(Plate_LXXVI)_(6140286962).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.767,
          "end": 20.9,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.894,
      "end": 28.814,
      "text": "Reaching the absolute peak of the scale, two-thirds of those massive neurological counts live directly inside its eight arms.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "\u0420\u0443\u043a\u0430 \u043c\u043e\u0440\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0433\u043e \u043f\u0440\u0438\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0430.jpg",
        "credit": "\u0410\u043d\u0434\u0440\u0435\u0439 \u0411\u0438\u043a\u0441\u0430\u043b\u0435\u0435\u0432",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BC%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B0.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.9,
          "end": 24.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.867,
          "end": 28.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.814,
      "end": 36.234,
      "text": "Each arm operates with semi-independence, tasting and touching without waiting for commands from the central brain.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Coconut octopus (Amphioctopus marginatus) (42825525034).jpg",
        "credit": "Rickard Zerpe",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coconut_octopus_(Amphioctopus_marginatus)_(42825525034).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 31.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 31.867,
          "end": 36.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.234,
      "end": 43.859,
      "text": "Some clever individuals even collect discarded coconut shells for portable shelter across the ocean floor.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Octopus marginatus.JPG",
        "credit": "Jens Petersen",
        "license": "CC BY 2.5",
